IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-rules`
IMPORT `wills-seat-family`

-- Wills Act 2000 (NT) -- worked cases for the questions of the person with an interest in a deceased person's will
-- (wills-seat-family.l4) and the date helpers.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the family and beneficiaries`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

-- February 2028 has 29 days (leap year), 2027 has 28; January 2027 runs 30 days from the 1st to the 31st.
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2028 EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2027 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the days in month` 12 `of` 2027 EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 1 2027) `to` (`d` 31 1 2027) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 16 3 2028
-- Six months after a day: the same day-number six months on, or the last day of a shorter month.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 12 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2028
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 7 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2028

§§ `s 54 -- can I see the will`

#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `an executor named in the will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a person entitled to apply for letters of administration with the will annexed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a person named or referred to in the will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `the deceased's surviving spouse` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `the deceased's child, grandchild or other issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a parent or guardian of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a person entitled to a share if the deceased had died without a will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a creditor or other person with a claim against the estate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a beneficiary of an earlier will of the deceased` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or entitled on intestacy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A de facto partner who is neither named nor entitled on intestacy is not in the list (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `the deceased's de facto partner, not named in the will and not entitled on intestacy` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I see the will` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 51(3), (4) -- can I have the deposited will`

#ASSERT `Can I have the deposited will` `an executor named in the will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I have the deposited will` `a person entitled to apply for letters of administration with the will annexed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I have the deposited will` `a person named or referred to in the will` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I have the deposited will` `the deceased's surviving spouse` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I have the deposited will` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10 -- can the Court accept the document as the will`

-- Arguments: properly executed, purports to embody testamentary intentions, the Court satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the document as the will` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the document as the will` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the document as the will` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court accept the document as the will` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 12 -- is my gift as a witness void`

-- Arguments: I witnessed, witnesses taking nothing, written consents, the Court satisfied of knowledge and approval, of freedom.
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 12 does not touch it: the beneficiary was not a witness`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void: at least 2 of the witnesses take nothing under the will (s 12(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void: at least 2 of the witnesses take nothing under the will (s 12(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, as far as it concerns the witness and anyone claiming under them (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void: everyone who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing (s 12(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not void: the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of it and gave it freely (s 12(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `void, as far as it concerns the witness and anyone claiming under them (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my gift as a witness void` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `void, as far as it concerns the witness and anyone claiming under them (s 12(1))`

§§ `s 27(1) -- can the will be rectified`

#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `a clerical error was made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the will be rectified` `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 27(2)-(4) -- by when, and is my application in time`

#ASSERT `By when must I apply for rectification` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for rectification` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028

-- Arguments: death, applied, applied on, today, the Court extended, finally distributed.
-- Death 10 January 2027; last day 10 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the time (s 27(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `out of time, but the Court has extended the time (s 27(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 27(4))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2027) (`d` 1 8 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `out of time, but the Court has extended the time (s 27(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 5 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still open: I can apply in time`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 7 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still open: I can apply in time`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 11 7 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the time (s 27(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 10 1 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 11 7 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 27(4))`
-- Death 31 August 2027; last day 29 February 2028 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 31 8 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my rectification application in time` (`d` 31 8 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) (`d` 1 4 2028) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `out of time: I need the Court to extend the time (s 27(3))`

§§ `ss 34, 40 -- surviving the will-maker by 30 days`

-- Will-maker died 1 March 2027: the 30th day after is 31 March, the 31st is 1 April.
#ASSERT `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027)
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027)))
#ASSERT `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027)
-- Across 29 February 2028: from 15 February the 30th day is 16 March.
#ASSERT `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 16 3 2028)
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 17 3 2028)))

§§ `ss 30, 34, 40, 41 -- what becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died`

-- Arguments: alive, will-maker died, beneficiary died, contrary intention, beneficiary was issue, own issue survived by 30
-- days, excluded (class gift to issue or a life interest), condition unmet, fractional share, the residue itself.
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 30(2), 34(2), 40(3), 41(3))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `held on trust for the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days (s 40(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `held on trust for the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days (s 40(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 30(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the failed part passes to the other fractional parts proportionately (s 41(2))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the failed part passes to the other fractional parts proportionately (s 41(2))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 30(1))`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Act does not say: a failed gift of the residue itself (intestacy law decides)`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the gift to a beneficiary who died` FALSE (`d` 15 2 2028) (`d` 17 3 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`

§§ `s 55 -- can the executor pay me maintenance now`

-- Arguments: dependent, entitlement not yet absolute, death, today. Death 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 28 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the executor pay me maintenance now` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 19-22 -- can the Court give leave for a will for my relative`

-- Arguments: alive, reason to believe incapable, would have made it, appropriate, appropriate applicant, represented.
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court give leave for a will for my relative` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
